{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/493824-utterances-as-story-hooks","id":493824,"title":"Utterances as Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-27T12:09:16-07:00","id":493824,"title":"Utterances as Story Hooks","content":"Recently I read something our resident power engineer/mad genius Nephipal said on the subject of his approach to designing Affinities and Utterances. The nuthshell of is that Affinities were designed to be a toolbox, powers you used to deal with common, every day sort of trouble you have as a Deathless, while Utterances were explicitly not Toolbox, and served more as player provided storyhooks for the GM.<br /> <br /> Which, is true. Most games don't demand a swarm of meteorites or an earthquake, but Mummy give you really huge abilities that allow a player to drastically shape a story.<br /> <br /> So, let's go with it. Pick some Utterances and create the scenarios that justify their use.<br /> <br /> BONUS ROUND: While there's no real reason to do so, let's also run with which Utterances are favored by each of the Deceived Temakhs, as a fun aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:26:20-07:00","id":493944,"title":"","content":"Define 'justify' in this case. Because I can think of excuses to use most of the really destructive ones in a lot of circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T14:44:00-07:00","id":493957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/493824-utterances-as-story-hooks?p=493944#post493944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define 'justify' in this case. Because I can think of excuses to use most of the really destructive ones in a lot of circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might just be your inner Exalted fan; after all, Shun the Smiling Lady is an appropriate response to everything.<br /> <br /> But more to the point of the thread: an alien invasion. Because Mummy vs. Aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T15:39:01-07:00","id":493983,"title":"","content":"One day that will make sense to me.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, create a scenario where using a given Utterance should inevitably come up. Now that I phrase it like this, it seems lame, sooooo.<br /> <br /> Your players pick these powers because they want to use them. Rose Bailey has put forth the solid game design principle of treating powers like plot twists and storyhooks.<br /> <br /> So, build some stories off of Utterances.<br /> <br /> As for Aliens, well, yeah. ID4 will always need Mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T16:50:21-07:00","id":494059,"title":"","content":"Chthonic Dominion and Words of Dead Hunger lend themselves to a story about constructing a legion of ghost soldiers by reforming the spirits of the dead. Of course, the question of how moral it is to fundamentally tear down the metaphysical underpinnings of a being and remake them into something new for no other reason than to further your own agenda (most obviously in the case of Words of Dead Hunger and its &quot;burn in a lake of fire&quot; schtick, but the more insidious brainwashing potential available through Chthonic Dominion's memory erasure is also notable) arise quite naturally.<br /> <br /> Before long, two rival Mummies could easily find themselves leading hosts through Neter-Khetet against one another. As the mortal world continues oblivious, its spectral counterpart becomes the scene of a battleground between legions of altered spirits. The echoes of lost lives or mournful protectors of their old family home have been remade into little more than ethereal cannon fodder for a war of the dead.<br /> <br /> Aaaand then someone unleashes Tier 3 Words of Dead Fury and things get messy very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T18:11:49-07:00","id":494180,"title":"","content":"California drought.<br /> <br /> Water of Life and Death.<br /> <br /> Say hello to your new cult and improved cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T19:01:30-07:00","id":494222,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Tier 3 Words of Dead Fury, the nature of a Chthonic Being is such that you can easily run stories around one bound to a location or otherwise constrained in its feeding choices by the one who summoned it. It needs to be getting a source of ghosts from somewhere... and bonus points if it has a clause in its binding that sets it free should it ever begin to starve.<br /> <br /> One idea that has always entertained me has been the thought of an Arisen using Gift of the Golden Ankh Tier 3 to try and get a sense of what Duat is like, by-passing the wall in their memories by sacrificing mortals and bringing them back shortly afterwards in the hopes that the vagaries of time in the real world and the afterlife will allow for the soul to witness Duat before it must be called back to life.<br /> <br /> Dreams of Dead Gods Tier 1 pretty much writes itself. The character is the monster of prophecy, whose coming brings horrifying dreams to those destined to oppose or aid it. When it wakes, it finds its cult assembled, and its enemies mustering just beyond the portal of its tomb.<br /> <br /> Palace Knows Its Pharaoh Tier 3 unleashed when Sekhem is 8 or higher, for when you want to fight alien gods on the surface of a dead world in the farthest reaches of the universe. Bonus points for unleashing Tier 3 Ancestry of Forgotten Stars prior to the fight, for a proper dose of Lovecraftian apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:51:02-07:00","id":494870,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars, tier 3... I've yet to figure out any way it could be useful without storing it for later use. I mean... the casting time makes it hard to pull off in a combat situation. It doesn't really last long enough to get anywhere, even with the warp powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:57:16-07:00","id":495161,"title":"","content":"Hilariously, I think it's more useful in order to ask the horror questions than it is to actually pull off in combat. But, if you can get within about a kilometre of a target before you cast it, you could well be able to warp close enough to do a lot of damage.<br /> <br /> That said, yeah, the hour long cast time and the duration being a matter of turns has always raised eyebrows amongst my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:59:45-07:00","id":496956,"title":"","content":"Well<br /> Tier 3 of AOFS is amazing if you know a fight is going to happen.<br /> This isn't just about prophecy power. Have the cult hold off the enemy for just a certain amount of time; tangentially, it's amazing for launching a siege or while under one - all you need is an hour, and then you have a doomsday entity on your side.<br /> I didn't think it was for use in single-combat. It thought it was about crushing an army, and there are a lot of situations where you have (or can buy) time in that kind of large-scale fight.<br /> <br /> As for a story built off an Utterance: any Tier of Words of Dead Glory. Every single one makes dozens of stories for a mortal/hunter game; every single one sets up a hook, event or NPC for later in a Mummy chronicle. You can even have these things show up from prior Descents; the Arisen <i>just forgot</i> about all those lifeless it made and left guarding a place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:16:05-07:00","id":496963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/493824-utterances-as-story-hooks?p=496956#post496956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well<br /> Tier 3 of AOFS is amazing if you know a fight is going to happen.<br /> This isn't just about prophecy power. Have the cult hold off the enemy for just a certain amount of time; tangentially, it's amazing for launching a siege or while under one - all you need is an hour, and then you have a doomsday entity on your side.<br /> I didn't think it was for use in single-combat. It thought it was about crushing an army, and there are a lot of situations where you have (or can buy) time in that kind of large-scale fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy story hook! &quot;Stop the ritual before the unstoppable crawling horror appears on their side.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I like most about Words of Dead Hunger Tier 3 is the fact that it doesn't compel obedience. I mean, on a metaphysical level you've changed the very anchors of a ghost's being into &quot;Destroy what is beautiful&quot;, &quot;Obey me&quot; and &quot;one other destructive command&quot;, so there's definitely the assumption that you've bent the ghost's will to your own, but it doesn't force it the way Tier 2 Chthonic Dominion does. So there's actually room for a ghost to fight its impulses (bonus points if its master has Striking Looks and it can get away with attacking said master due to the &quot;Destroy what is beautiful&quot; passion) and turn its newfound powers against its master. Lots of stories could abound from angry fire spirits who decide to resent that whole &quot;trapped in a lake of fire&quot; schtick they were subjected to.<br /> <br /> Hm. I also like the idea of combining Word of the Amanuensis with that Affinity from Book of the Deceived that causes the Mummy's name to inflict Sybaris. A sacred text with instructions to wake the Arisen coupled with the first two Tiers of the Utterance alongside the Mummy's name, and you have a tool that could drive mortals who see it to try and bring you to life. Or if that's not the kind of thing you want to do, insert any other mission you would want Sybaris-inflicted mortals to go about doing without requiring your direct intervention. &quot;The book made me do it!&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there's the classic idea of creating a maze of doom using a combination of Palace Knows Its Pharaoh Tier 3, Kiss of Apep Tier 3, and Awaken the Dead Tier 2 (since Awakened Servants are Strength 7 in a tomb and last forever). Mad, physics-defying insanity that moves in and out of Twilight and involves occasional rabid zombie attacks. Drop some mortals inside and watch the fun.<br /> <br /> Finally, this is a favourite of mine. It's less about the power of the Utterance itself, and more about what it implies. What if a Tef-Aabhi Flesh Mason found out about the underlying metaphysics of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars and decided to breed a population specifically to try and bring out the demonic traits that the Su-Menent are tapping into with that Utterance (possibly with help from Seeds of Life Tier 3). What if <i>someone already did</i>, and the breeding has been going on for centuries? What sort of horror is about to be born into the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}